Source landscape: The documentary universe is broad enough for 1B. It spans Türkiye’s treaty and safeguards records, IAEA/UN/CTBTO materials, nuclear-regulatory and energy records, NATO nuclear-sharing assessments, Turkish cyber and biosafety policy, academic and legal analysis, think-tank assessments, Erdoğan’s public rhetoric, and local-language reporting. The strongest source families concern Akkuyu’s governance and safeguards, Türkiye’s NATO nuclear-hosting role, nonproliferation commitments, cyber strategy, and dual-use biological-risk regulation. Several candidates are metadata-only, paywalled, or retrospective and should be inspected later.

